# Contract v1.3: the composition shows only in the panel's input line (pinyin with syllable spaces, a draft as
# "improve › ok"), never as marked text in the field; the field gets text only on commit.
# Tab while pinyin is typed belongs to the input method: rime-ice's key_binder sends it on as Shift+Right (the cursor
# to the next syllable; rime-ice's default.yaml, fetched into ThirdParty/rime-data: "Tab / Shift+Tab 切换光标至下/上一个拼音"), and the Rime
# wrapper lists Tab among the keys that edit the composition and never commit it (RimeSession.editingKeys). Nothing goes
# in, the focus stays, the pinyin stays in the panel's input line (contract v1.3: never marked in the field) and its
# candidates stay up. (Tab inserting a row is the other panels':
# the command list, suggestions, clipboard history, the user guide's "Every panel works the same way".) Seen on a real
# Mac 2026-11-15: the marked text stayed "nihao" (then still shown inline).
# QUESTION: `EXPECT preedit` can pin the input line's caret with a `|`, but where librime leaves it after Tab at the
# end of "ni hao" (rime-ice: Shift+Right, "to the next syllable") isn't verified on a real Mac, so it isn't pinned.
NAME Tab during pinyin stays with the input method: nothing goes in and the pinyin stays in the panel
PROFILES all
LANG chinese
TEXT "Hi |"
TYPE nihao
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT preedit "ni hao"
EXPECT panel shown
KEY tab
EXPECT doc "Hi "
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT preedit "ni hao"
EXPECT panel shown
